course: dictionary
lesson: 3929
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word fruit is a good example. «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» Here fruit means the sweet, juicy food you eat, like an apple or a banana.
explain: Scientists use fruit in a special way. In science, a fruit is any part of a flowering plant that grows from the flower and holds seeds, so a tomato counts as a fruit too. Ask yourself: is this sentence about food, or about a plant and its seeds?
explain: Fruit can also be a verb, which means to make fruit. The word has a third meaning too: the fruits of work are its good results. If you spend weeks practising and then win a race, the win is one of the fruits of your practice.
fact: Fruit is the sweet or juicy part of a plant that holds seeds and that you can eat.
fact: «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» Here fruit means food.
fact: In science, a fruit is any part of a flowering plant that grows from the flower and holds seeds.
fact: Tomatoes and peppers are fruits in science, even though we often cook them like vegetables.
fact: «Fruits» means kinds of fruit, as in «How many fruits are on the table?»
fact: «The fruits of work» means the good results of work.
exercise: «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» What is fruit in this sentence? | Food that is sweet and juicy | *Food that is sweet and juicy, like an apple | A seat for the sports team | A kind of cereal
exercise: In science, which of these is a fruit? | Root | Stem | *Tomato | Leaf
exercise: «In the flooded forest fish like the tambaqui eat fallen fruit and nuts and spread the seeds.» Find and copy one word that is a food. | *fruit | spread | forest | seeds
test: «The apple tree began to fruit in June.» What does fruit mean in this sentence? | To sing loudly | To pick up | To fall down | *To make fruit
test: «The fruits of her hard practice were a gold medal.» What does fruits mean here? | Seeds in the ground | Juicy plants | Kinds of food | *Good results
exam: Which phrase means the good results of hard work? | *the fruits of hard work | a fruit salad | fresh fruit juice | a fruit bowl
